    {
      "id": "f7cef1aeac5d023d265ec1e71fbcb051be9f0108",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 1543215761,
          "type": null,
          "body": "What about other formats, like `CEST`?",
          "author": {
            "id": 4753670,
            "username": "stigbjorlykke",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Stig Bjørlykke",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/905aafc6b50e246885f5ea9273a9dc4f22e2658b71f9a1b551b797082bec3f80?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/stigbjorlykke"
          },
          "created_at": "2023-09-05T06:41:56.697Z",
          "updated_at": "2023-09-05T06:41:56.697Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 247499842,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": false,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 11947,
          "commands_changes": {}
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "3cd45825cd7319af3e4d16871837ffd10e5f0ccf",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 1543275894,
          "type": null,
          "body": "> What about other formats, like `CEST`?\n\nOr `PST`, or `WET`, or....\n\n\"UTC\" is easy to support - convert the time as UTC rather than as local time.\n\n*Arbitrary* other time zones are harder, because:\n\n1. there's no general API that can be made to work on arbitrary UN\\*Xes and Windows for specifying \"convert this in a time zone other than local time or UTC\";\n2. converting from a time zone abbreviation to the corresponding time zone is, in the general case, a one-to-many mapping.\n\nThe *test* is using `WET` as a test that it *fails*; I'm not sure we'd need to test whether `CEST` or `PST` or... fails as well.",
          "author": {
            "id": 5636682,
            "username": "guyharris",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Guy Harris",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/1b7c243a9b1d6587a9a9067e5d83aba1e87212df7c4eeae3690f791ecbe4675a?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/guyharris"
          },
          "created_at": "2023-09-05T07:27:52.679Z",
          "updated_at": "2023-09-05T07:27:52.679Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 247499842,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": false,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 11947,
          "commands_changes": {}
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "98afb1896b7c54b00167bf16e3d55bec6f93d689",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 1543609128,
          "type": null,
          "body": "> What about other formats, like `CEST`?\n\n!11951 adds support for the timezones ws_strptime() already knows about (some US timezones).\n\nIt wouldn't be difficult to extend %z to know about other common timezones, for example European, but I don't have plans to work on this.\n\nI don't want to get too deep into it either with Olson databases or whatever, we already support UTC time offsets, timezones are messy, it's just a nice to have.",
          "author": {
            "id": 2639362,
            "username": "jvalverde",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "João Valverde",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/bea5f745397cf5a2fe0526df96ec143db47f9334340ab56515038832be57e976?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/jvalverde"
          },
          "created_at": "2023-09-05T10:32:05.895Z",
          "updated_at": "2023-09-05T10:32:05.895Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 247499842,
